a/1760233/000149315225004034/0001493152-25-004034-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-01-21","form":"8-K","codes":["1.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Material agreement entered","kind":"deal","tone":"good"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315225003086/0001493152-25-003086-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[],"summary":{"sentences":["GIFTIFY, INC. files with the SEC under \"Retail-Catalog & Mail-Order Houses\", based in IL, and has been publicly reporting for 3 years.","It reported $83.3m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, down 4.1% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 19.9%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($71.7k of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 16.1% to 19.9% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315226022415/0001493152-26-022415-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022415"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $71.7k over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315226022415/0001493152-26-022415-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022415"},{"text":"Net cash of $4.2m against total assets of $31.0m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315226022415/0001493152-26-022415-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022415"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 4.1% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315226022415/0001493152-26-022415-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022415"},{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 778.1% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315226022415/0001493152-26-022415-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022415"},{"text":"Gross margin is only 19.9%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315226022415/0001493152-26-022415-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022415"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-12.5% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315226022415/0001493152-26-022415-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022415"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 18.4% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1760233/000149315226022415/0001493152-26-022415-index.htm","accession":"0001493152-26-022415"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 12.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.12,"consecutive":2,"current":0.199,"current_display":"19.9%","threshold_display":"12.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -19.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.19,"consecutive":2,"current":-0.041,"current_display":"-4.1%","threshold_display":"-19.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 25.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.25,"consecutive":1,"current":0.184,"current_display":"18.4%","threshold_display":"25.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.0,"current_display":"0.00","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","comparison":"is_true","threshold":true,"current":false,"current_display":"not present","fired":false,"rationale":"The auditors saying the company may not survive the year is not a signal to interpret. It is the exit.","editable":false}],"team":[{"raw_name":"Thakker Ketan","role":"Officer","title_filed":"CEO","shares":3461098.0,"sold_in_window":0.0,"bought_in_window":1000.0,"last_filing":"2026-02-24","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001760233","confidence":"filed","prior_companies":[]},{"raw_name":"Ackerman Ari Marc","role":"Officer","title_filed":"COO, CardCash Exchange, Inc.","shares":1136109.0,"sold_in_window":0.0,"bought_in_window":0.0,"last_filing":"2026-03-23","source_url":"https://ww